map_=dict(version=1,target_profile=dict(system_boundary='Captured EPaxos implementation plus in-repository replica transport, static master configuration, state execution and client admission. Other protocol packages are outside this initial map.',protocol_contexts=['Per-origin instance rows and ballots; fixed membership; thriftiness enabled by constructor'],external_interfaces=['TCP typed peer RPCs','Client PROPOSE/ProposeReplyTS','Master registration and BeTheLeader RPC'],source_ids=['M-init','M-run','M-replica','M-listener']),activities=activities,behaviors=bs,facts=[fact],surfaces=[],core_overview=dict(status='usable',formation=path('A1: A client proposal is batched by its receiving replica into a local-row instance. Conflict indexes supply sequence/dependencies; thriftiness selects a preferred live peer subset. PreAccept replies are filtered by attempted ballot and phase, then counted/merged. Fast conditions commit directly; otherwise Accept replies at matching ballot establish the coordinator commit threshold. Commit broadcasts carry commands and attributes. Recipients install guarded committed records. Dependency/SCC execution waits for prerequisite commands and committed status, applies ordered operations and answers deferred clients.',['B-form','B-accept','B-commit','B-execute','B-client','B-config'],['M-phase1','M-accept','M-send','M-commit','M-exec','M-replica']),context=path('A2: Authority is per instance, not exclusive global proposal leadership. Initial ballots equal origin replica ID. Recovery resets bookkeeping while retaining client proposals/value context, selects a ballot, adds a self reply and sends Prepare. Acceptors raise their promise and export prior value ballot/status. The recovering coordinator collects matching replies and selects a highest-value-ballot tuple before committing locally, accepting or restarting phase1. Lower-ballot requests and nonmatching replies are guarded. Complete committed records skip recovery. Master designation affects higher-ballot retry but does not stop other replicas proposing.',['B-context','B-recover-trigger','B-config'],['M-recovery','M-ballot','M-commit','M-master','M-dispatch']),connection=path('A1/A2 connection: The record status and value ballot exported by Prepare determine whether earlier formation support constrains the new attempt as committed, accepted or merely preaccepted. Reset bookkeeping discards old counts; phase and ballot checks constrain delayed replies. Accepted/committed follower guards limit new PreAccept modifications, while delayed Commit is rejected below a newer promise. Pending local client proposals survive recovery and may be reproposed after NOOP. Execution later consumes the selected record, so retention of support classification matters independently of client visibility.',['B-form','B-accept','B-context','B-commit','B-execute'],['M-phase1','M-accept','M-recovery','M-commit','M-exec']),core_gaps=[],open_details=['Follower Accept leaves Status unchanged; investigate preservation through Prepare.','Prepare selection overwrites equal-VBallot tuples in reply order; recoverer also rewrites self vbal before exporting it.','TryPreAccept recovery subcase has duplicate condition after the prior branch; deeper reachability remains open.','Transport queues per message asynchronously; legal dispatch histories and shared-memory observations need question-specific review.','Fault/restart and client retry contracts remain incomplete.'],rationale='Representative formation, authority transition, old-work guards and consumption are traced with source-backed unresolved local discrepancies; no correctness or coverage claim.'))
